t{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,x\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-y}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $R$ as a type III region and its projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane as a type I *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $y$-axis and in the direction of increasing $y,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/c48de52085373361c4e4de3010ebe36c1da702f0efec45b455dff891869086f2.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the left boundary and leaves through the right boundary:\n\n- The left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x,z),$ is\n\n$$\nx=y\\,⟹\\,y=x\n$$\n\n- The right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nz=1-y\\,⟹\\,y=1-z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,x\\le y\\le 1-z},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/fd5d71a6d6509851e5131fe458b9672d59eb7ff6c07499949ae199b45f4ddae0.png)\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xz$-plane with the top curve given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=1-z \\\\ y=x\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,x=1-z\\,⟹\\,z=1-x.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/12743c492a7f7883a2ecd8d3ca73138a324a53040cb8936f4794f9e8d84c8fd5.png)\n\nHence, we have that\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration so that it is integrated first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-y}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{x}^{1-z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379556 13194139536016 true] [17592186379555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379557 13194139536016 true] [17592186379555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379558 13194139536016 true] [17592186379555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379559 13194139536016 true] [17592186379555 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379560 13194139536016 true] [17592186379555 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536016 true] [17592186379555 1041 "selection" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379555 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379558 13194139536016 true] [17592186379555 1110 #uuid "c69b9535-37b3-5f87-b0de-86953b3ee6ef" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379556 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{1-z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379556 1111 #uuid "a47f237d-c9ef-518a-8d24-152bdb99afec" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379557 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{z}^{1-x}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379557 1111 #uuid "dc197835-26dc-5181-a675-84dadfaf4c94" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379558 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{x}^{1-z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379558 1111 #uuid "1d445e2e-678b-5818-8d7b-d02e0ca8d579" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379559 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{0}^{z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379559 1111 #uuid "d7a6c30d-de22-5640-bab2-f