73682/assets/58a9056015b3dad91ec7ae64bff893c8c6c2cce6480c979545e423cbe105ef03.png)\n\nThen, the region $R$ is shown in the diagram below, where ${y}^{3}\\le z\\le 2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/2fdd6a15b4ddadfc3ee24af5e35e2a87e9e963ceeefbf858b704d78ee0b78513.png)\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $R$ as a type III region and its projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane as a type I *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $y$-axis and in the direction of increasing $y,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/65da730d32f200b8f9da004ee8cf6b7e79095e323961f4a5b6dfa0bddeace42b.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the left boundary and leaves through the right boundary:\n\n- The right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=(x,z),$ is\n\n$$\nz={y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt[3]{z}\n$$\n\n- The left boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{z}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/1743f540a85fc1c266c84da8f34b2012516b7bbc98d113cf7c62ba3bba8173c1.png)\n\nWe now consider the projection $D$ as a type II plane region in the $xz$-plane with the top curve given by \n\n$$\nz=(\\sqrt[3]{2})^{3}=2.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/b76bf84e1179bec6a1e8e357c6cc628eee95c1663e6f0ff375135612a6f275de.png)\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{2},\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{2}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{z}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379570 13194139536016 true] [17592186379569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379571 13194139536016 true] [17592186379569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379572 13194139536016 true] [17592186379569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379573 13194139536016 true] [17592186379569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379574 13194139536016 true] [17592186379569 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536016 true] [17592186379569 1041 "selection" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379569 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379571 13194139536016 true] [17592186379569 1110 #uuid "21dfee99-4f2c-57af-b8d9-c72c538620a6" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379570 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[3]{z+1}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379570 1111 #uuid "9b03a5e1-3023-5f5e-8777-575db44c7214" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379571 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{z}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379571 1111 #uuid "b3efbfcf-f3ff-5a57-8033-7e36832528a9" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379572 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{3}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379572 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379572 1111 #uuid "ed50618c-72bf-52fc-b4c2-39827e54c21b" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379573 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{1}^{{z}^{3}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379573 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379573 1111 #uuid "4394a865-b272-59f0-8147-754452a47b47" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379574 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{z}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379574 1111 #uuid "96b72c4b-f7e3-5c69-911d-9614d7e035b5" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379575 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379576 13194139536016 true] [17592186379575 1089 "q-163222" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379575 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536016 true] [17592186379575 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/63118a7b3d7fd589513f41ae1e721baf25305f480e683c984088fedb9a8d759b.png)\n\nChange the order of integration in the integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nso that it is integrated first with respect to $x,$ then over a region $D$ in the $yz$-plane. The integration region $R$ is shown above." 13194139536016 true] [17592186379575 1113 #uuid "254fbc86-e0b9-5007-8b84-f491c3555b5f" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379575 1145 "We wish to find the limits of integration ${u}_{1}(y,z)$ and ${u}_{2}(y,z)$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type III region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,\\,:\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}A,$ we write $R$ as a type II region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $x$-axis and in the direction of increasing $x,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/7dbabd349afb41c00c447ab61e28139cc7818a74c54bd17a61eb77d05ae558ae.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the back boundary and leaves through the front boundary:\n\n- The front boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y,z),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- The back boundary of the region is $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,\\,:\\,\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/4040e2d2eadc5c39b9224b1b39980de486fe6dd69dad1e63179c6cffcb4046b4.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration so that it is integrated first with respect to $x$ and then over $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379577 13194139536016 true] [17592186379576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379578 13194139536016 true] [17592186379576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379579 13194139536016 true] [17592186379576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379580 13194139536016 true] [17592186379576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379581 13194139536016 true] [17592186379576 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536016 true] [17592186379576 1041 "selection" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379576 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379580 13194139536016 true] [17592186379576 1110 #uuid "ee9bcaeb-4b04-5e34-aebd-d30064ec5e1f" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379577 1034 "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A" 13194139536016 