583 1111 #uuid "dff45150-2ba4-5086-939f-09baf7641382" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379584 1034 "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{2-z}^{(2-x-z)/2}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379584 1111 #uuid "5e866a3f-2ce6-52d9-89ff-c7a6f8deba26" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379585 1034 "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{(2-x-z)/2}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379585 1111 #uuid "b0b85c41-66b6-5b13-bffb-fc8574503bc6" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379586 1034 "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x-z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379586 1111 #uuid "cd6431ac-5b19-5e26-90fb-6f94a71a212a" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379587 1034 "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{2-x-z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379587 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379587 1111 #uuid "b6eb66b8-3996-5a66-89a4-23aee607d73b" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379588 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379589 13194139536016 true] [17592186379588 1089 "q-38982" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379588 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536016 true] [17592186379588 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/446e61491ae43e610dc39e4b46b752668969540f7733bf7d9c945fa260210a77.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.$ The region of integration is shown above.\n\n*Hint: Change the order of integration to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.$*" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379588 1113 #uuid "c570f574-3af8-5e51-88f9-850621146869" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379588 1145 "We cannot integrate the given integral because we cannot find a simple antiderivative of the integrand. So, we change the order of integration.\n\nWe wish to find the limits of integration ${u}_{1}(x,z),$ ${u}_{2}(x,z),$ ${v}_{1}(x),$ ${v}_{2}(x),$ $a,$ and $b$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,y\\le z\\le 1}\n$$\n\nThe region $R$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/b486ea542dc330a483fa76f333ab80c9fcd07434db5dc0c5a0a62a335294f127.png)\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $R$ as a type III region and its projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane as a type I *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $y$-axis and in the direction of increasing $y,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/b626c20c336bc81df9194f161998f7c6aea524a11495fede615cdf76f5d93f59.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the left boundary and leaves through the right boundary:\n\n- The left boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\n- The right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x,z),$ is\n\n$$\nz=y\\,⟹\\,y=z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le z},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/7386453aebec047469c829e2c2c5d6c4ab915ac965bbcd39838dc7be50941d54.png)\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xz$-plane with the bottom curve given by $z=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073682/assets/4b2bb3583b5c0807c653f503cdf9ed954f38db8a30eef548738e96cedb889288.png)\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}[y]_{0}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{1}{3}{(1-{z}^{2})}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379590 13194139536016 true] [17592186379589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379591 13194139536016 true] [17592186379589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379592 13194139536016 true] [17592186379589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379593 13194139536016 true] [17592186379589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379594 13194139536016 true] [17592186379589 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536016 true] [17592186379589 1041 "selection" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379589 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379594 13194139536016 true] [17592186379589 1110 #uuid "993c9132-301f-500f-92e3-f70e8476fc80" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379590 1034 "\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379590 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536016 true] [17592186379590 1111 #uuid "eda6ae21-370a-5048-84c3-7f7739e3cc66" 13194139536016 true] [17592186379591 1034 "\\frac{2}{